{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>He who offers it as a sin-offering.</b> The one who performs its service — for through his hand it becomes a sin-offering." "<b>He who offers it as a sin-offering shall eat it.</b> The one fit for the service — excluding one who was impure at the time of the blood-sprinkling, who does not share in the flesh. And it is impossible to say that he prohibits other priests from eating it apart from the one who sprinkles its blood, for below it is stated: ״כָּל זָכָר בַּכֹּהֲנִים יֹאכַל אֹתָהּ״ (Zevaḥim 99b)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:20.585305547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}